   "value": "## Conclusion\n\nWrite `V_site1 = adjoint (x) det` as traceless 3x3 matrices (`Sum_i E_ii = 3` forces the `det`\nfactor). A covector is then a matrix `Y` via `Tr[Y M_k] = w_k`. For `w = (0,0,cc,0,bb,0,aa,1)`:\n\n```\n        [ -bb/6   aa/2   1/3  ]\n   Y =  [   0    -bb/6    0   ]  =  (1/3) E13 + (aa/2) E12 + (bb/6) H + cc E32,\n        [   0      cc    bb/3 ]                      H = diag(-1,-1,2)\n```\n\n### Why no group element works\n\n`g` in `GL(3)` acts by conjugation, so **rank and spectrum are invariants**. The reference `<e8|`\nis `Y_8 = E13/3`: rank one, `Y_8^2 = 0` — the minimal nilpotent orbit. But\n\n```\n   Det Y = bb^3/108 ,     charpoly = (bb - 3t)(bb + 6t)^2 / 108\n```\n\nso for `bb != 0` the object is **invertible**. It is not `<e8| g` for *any* `g` in `GL(3)`, let alone\na unipotent one. Directly (cell 17): `<e8| exp(x E21 + y E31 + z E32)` has slot 6 `= x` and slot 1\n`= -y^2/3`, so matching the zeros forces `x = y = 0`, leaving only the one-parameter `E32` rotation\n(the `aa` direction).\n\n### What it is instead\n\nThe four localized directions span a **4-dimensional Lie subalgebra** of `gl(3)` — span plus all 16\ncommutators still has rank 4 — namely the **oscillator algebra**\n\n```\n   a  = E13              (slot 8, coefficient 1 )      [a, a+] = c\n   a+ = E32              (slot 3, coefficient cc)      [c, a ] = [c, a+] = 0\n   c  = E12              (slot 7, coefficient aa)      [H, a] = -3a, [H, a+] = +3a+, [H, c] = 0\n   H  = diag(-1,-1,2)    (slot 5, coefficient bb)\n```\n\ni.e. a 3-dimensional **Heisenberg algebra** `{a, a+, c = [a,a+]}` together with its **grading /\nnumber operator** `H`. The localized covector is a *general element of this algebra*, not the image\nof the reference covector under a group element. `H` is the grading element of the maximal parabolic\n`gl(2) (+) gl(1)` splitting off index 3; `c = E12` spans the one direction both `a` and `a+` miss.\n\n### The one exception\n\n`Y` is semisimple — hence `bb` times a rotated **zero-weight (Cartan)** covector `<5|` — iff the\n`2x2` minors of `Y + (bb/6) 1` vanish:\n\n```\n   cc = (3/4) aa bb .\n```\n\nOff that surface `Y` carries a `2x2` Jordan block at the doubled eigenvalue `-bb/6`, and is\nconjugate to `(bb/6) H + E12`. Nilpotent limits: `bb = 0` (regular nilpotent if `cc != 0`), and\n`bb = cc = 0` (minimal nilpotent — the known local `E32` rotation).\n\n**To check next:** whether `adj (x) fund` populates the same four slots `{3,5,7,8}`, hence the same\noscillator algebra.",
